        "subject": "LU-21183 mdt: allow fid2path on an MDT mount",
        "message": "LU-21183 mdt: allow fid2path on an MDT mount\n\nTools on a server node need a client mount to turn a FID into a\npathname, and a client mount on a server causes trouble with HA\nfailover and module removal.\n\nLet OBD_IOC_FID2PATH work on an MDT's own mount point, with the\nsame struct getinfo_fid2path as on a client mount.  The target\nmount passes it to mdt_iocontrol(), which also takes it from\n/dev/obd.  With no client to continue the walk on another MDT, a\nremote object is read through OSP, with its cache dropped since no\nlock is held, so one MDT mount names any FID in the filesystem.\nEncrypted names return -ENODATA, since only a client can encode\nthem.\n\n\"lfs fid2path\" accepts an MDT mount point, found by statfs() and\nthe new LL_SERVER_SUPER_MAGIC, and prints the path from the\nfilesystem root, as it does when given the fsname.\n\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie25164aa8283b7266c512b1e72be5a95db83a5e1\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
